# Same reason as the v32 three above (912e004): data/ is bind-mounted into
# the running containers, so a committed measurement dump under it breaks
# CI's git reset on the deploy host. v33's numbers live in
# docs/superpowers/plans/implemented/v33-train-preregistration.md; these are the raw
# dumps they were read from, re-derivable from the two scripts named there.
#
# A GLOB rather than the three named files (v33_trend_overlap / v33_train /
# v33_validation), because the deploy breakage this prevents is caused by ANY
# new dump under data/, and the ad-hoc ones are exactly the ones nobody
# remembers to list -- Task 7's own reproducibility re-run wrote a fourth
# (data/v33_train_verify.json) that three explicit lines would have missed.
data/v33_*.json
# Same reason and same glob shape for v34's RS-gate measurement dumps
# (data/v34_train.json, data/v34_train_rows.json, data/v34_validation.json).
# The numbers live in
# docs/superpowers/plans/implemented/v34-train-preregistration.md;
# these are the raw dumps they were read from, re-derivable by re-running
# scripts/backtest/measure_rs_gate_effect.py.
data/v34_*.json

# Same reason again (912e004; v33 above generalized it to a glob) --
# data/v35_validation.json and data/v35_validation_off.json were briefly
# tracked and reproduced the identical deploy breakage. Numbers are
# reconciled in prose in
# docs/superpowers/plans/implemented/v35-avwap-preregistration.md sections
# 5.2-5.3. Extension-less (not `*.json` like v33) because v35's scratch
# also includes run logs, shell scripts and summary .txt dumps under the
# same prefix -- all equally unwanted under a bind-mounted data/.
data/v35_*

# Noisy raw run logs only -- narrowed from a blanket docs/superpowers/results/
# rule (fafcdc9) that hid the whole directory, including *.md/*.json validation
# deliverables the backtest methodology in CLAUDE.md requires be committed.
# Caught when Task E80's results doc silently failed to `git add`.
docs/superpowers/results/*.log

# pytest scratch: .pytest-last-run.log is where scripts/dev/testrun.py parks full
# pytest output so only its 1-3 line verdict reaches the caller's context.
.pytest_cache/
.pytest-last-run.log

# Angular SPA (sub-project 4). `frontend/` has its own .gitignore from
# `ng new`; these are here as well because the root file is where anyone
# looks, and because static/app/ is OUTSIDE frontend/ and its own file
# therefore cannot cover it.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.angular/
# The built SPA, copied here by the Dockerfile's frontend stage (NG33) and
# served by Flask. A build artefact -- never committed, or the image would
# ship whichever bundle someone last built by hand.
swingbot/admin/static/app/

# Brainstorming visual-companion sessions: mockups and server state, not source.
.superpowers/
